        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/sandboxed_writer.py:319-322 (`srt_launcher` only builds the npx argv); launch_sandboxed_writer passes `extra_env={TOKEN_ENV: token}` at :503-505, so the token goes to the outer process. design.md says: \"or a resolvable `srt` binary whose `--version` matches; a mismatch is an explicit refusal\".",
                  "id": "npx-runs-with-token-before-sandbox",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The outer `npx --yes @anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime@<ver>` process, and anything npx fetches or runs, starts with `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in its environment before the sandbox is applied. The version is pinned, but there is no integrity check. Design.md also promises a resolvable `srt` binary whose"
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/sandboxed_writer.py:459-467",
                  "id": "srt-tmp-mode-not-verified",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "`srt_tmp` sets mode 0700 only when it creates the directory. When `/private/tmp/dp-srt-<uid>` already exists, it checks that it is a directory and that the current user owns it, but not that its mode is 0700. A pre-existing looser mode is accepted. A race between `exists()` and `mkdir` is also unhan"
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/sandboxed_writer.py:348-357 and build_profile `deny_read` at :403-404",
                  "id": "protected-set-snapshot-at-launch",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The protected paths come from `git worktree list` once, at launch. Worktrees that sibling tasks create during a long writer run are not in `denyRead`. Writes stay safe because `allowWrite` is a whitelist, but the writer can read those worktrees. The model-routing doc describes \"every registered work"
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/sandboxed_writer.py:433 vs :479-483; :439-446",
                  "id": "token-path-expanduser-vs-operator-home",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The token path is expanded with `os.path.expanduser`, which uses the inherited `HOME`. The profile's home-relative entries use the account-database home instead (`operator_home()`). If `HOME` is overridden, a `~/` token_file may resolve differently from the deny entries, though the token file itself"
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
              "report_sha256": "c690ab6d3fc9a29097ecf948690c76983e1b7e335c0655b7a0ce5b61d8d86dd3"
            },
            "spec-fidelity": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "design.md says the launcher uses `npx --yes ...@<pinned>` \"or a resolvable `srt` binary whose `--version` matches; a mismatch is an explicit refusal\". The spec says the launch is refused \"when the pinned sandbox runtime ... is unavailable\". `template/scripts/sandboxed_writer.py` `srt_launcher()` (diff lines 319-322) checks only `shutil.which(\"npx\")` and returns the npx command. It never resolves an `srt` binary or checks its version. A failure to fetch or run the runtime would surface only as a ",
                  "id": "pinned-runtime-availability-not-checked",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The design and spec require an explicit refusal when the pinned sandbox runtime is unavailable or mismatched. The launcher only checks that `npx` is on PATH and does not verify the runtime itself."
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "spec-fidelity",
              "report_sha256": "27b73b1d4d7877544e6ad03b4913e418fe56484a7b53df379d1b300d105dd749"
            }
          },
