        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/model_routing.py `run_claude_sandboxed` creates `workdir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(...))`. The `except SandboxedWriterError -> RoutingError` path and the `prepare_sandboxed_checkout` failure path raise without cleanup. `dispatch_claude_sandboxed` only calls `shutil.rmtree(run[\"workdir\"])` on `completed`, so a pre-launch refusal (for example non-macOS) leaves the copy in the system temp dir.",
                  "id": "workdir-leak-on-prelaunch-failure",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The disposable workdir created by `tempfile.mkdtemp` is never removed when the dispatch fails before launch, or when the launcher raises. It holds a full copy of the task worktree including uncommitted state."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "`_sandboxed_claude_completed` (model_routing.py) checks only `mechanism`, `launch_evidence`, `launched`, `outcome`, `returncode` and the presence of a `participant` dict. `require_routing_gate` then returns the route, skipping the clean containment postcheck that the native Claude path requires. Because the gate bypasses the postcheck, the evidence it relies on is no longer cross-checked against the delegation record or the patch hash.",
                  "id": "gate-trusts-execution-fields-alone",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The new gate branch accepts any Claude execution whose JSON fields match the sandboxed shape. It does not check that a closed platform-observed delegation exists, that the patch evidence is present, or that the task content matches the applied patch."
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
              "report_sha256": "b107cf21d11c533410092b4a8cbd21c263812e3be302bfbf954cb905402f3d9e"
            },
